-- title:
--   p-th powers of principal units: (U^{(k)})ᵖ = U^{(k+e)} for k>e
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and which is complete with respect to the adic filtration by its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R`. Let $p$ be a prime number, and let $e$ be a natural number such that the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$ in $R$ equals $\mathfrak m^e$. Let $k$ be a natural number with $e < k$. Here, for a natural number $j$, `principalUnits R j` denotes the subgroup of $R^\times$ consisting of those units $u$ with $(u : R) - 1 \in \mathfrak m^{j}$. The assertion is an equality of subgroups of $R^\times$: the image of `principalUnits R k` under the monoid endomorphism $u \mapsto u^p$ of $R^\times$ equals `principalUnits R (k + e)`. Thus raising to the $p$-th power carries the $k$-th principal-unit subgroup onto, and not merely into, the $(k+e)$-th one, under the stated hypotheses that $p$ generates $\mathfrak m^e$ and that $k$ exceeds $e$.
--
--   This is the standard surjectivity statement in the theory of the filtration of units of a complete discrete valuation ring: above the ramification bound $k > e$, where $(p) = \mathfrak m^{e}$, the $p$-th power map moves the principal-unit filtration exactly $e$ steps. It is the input to the computation of the index of $p$-th powers in the group of principal units, and is used in the project's analysis of ramification in the local setting, where it is cited by [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.exists_ramification_principalUnits_Rw`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.exists_ramification_principalUnits_Rw).
-- source:
